Build a complete retro arcade Snake game in HTML/CSS/JavaScript with neon aesthetic in a single HTML file. The game offers three distinct render modes switchable via 1/2/3 keys or start-screen buttons.

**Core Gameplay (all modes):**
- 20×20 grid, 24px cells (2D/2.5D); 20×20 board with perspective camera (3D)
- Snake starts center with 3 segments facing right; arrow keys/WASD control (camera-relative in 3D)
- Input buffer: up to 2 queued moves; prevent 180° turns and duplicates
- Food spawns randomly; collision adds 1 segment, scores 10 points
- Speed: start 150ms per move, subtract 4ms per food (min 55ms)
- Death on wall collision or self-collision (tail safe if growing); screen shake on death (420ms decay, ±10px)

**Three Render Modes:**
- **2D:** Classic flat neon game (untouched from original)
- **2.5D:** Same board through perspective tilt + depth shading (isometric-style 3D-ified view)
- **3D:** Full perspective 3D with orbitable camera (drag to rotate, scroll to zoom); 3D board, floating arena with glowing rim, lighting and shadows
- Mode selection on INSERT COIN start screen; switchable anytime via 1/2/3 keys
- One persistent high score shared across all modes; remember last-used mode in localStorage

**Power-Ups (all modes):**
- Yuzu Berry (yellow/green orb): slow-mo (1.8× tick multiplier) for 6 seconds
- Ghost Star (white 5-point star, cyan glow): phase through self for 6 seconds
- Spawn every 6–13 seconds, exist 9 seconds, blink when <1.5s remain
- Power-up HUD badges (center) with countdown timers (0.0s format); blink near expiry
- Particle bursts (14 pink/yellow particles) on grab; sound: ascending triple beep (740→990→1240 Hz) for star, double beep for yuzu

**Visual Style (Neon Arcade Everywhere):**
- Dark background (#05050a); Press Start 2P font (chunky retro)
- Neon palette: green (#39ff14), pink (#ff2ec4), cyan (#00f0ff), yellow (#ffee00)
- **2D:** Cyan glowing canvas border, faint grid overlay; snake head cyan with glow, body fades green; food pulsing pink diamond; chunky pixel eyes on head; 32% opacity canvas clearing for trails
- **2.5D/3D:** Perspective board with depth shading (farther = darker); dark arena background; glowing cyan rim; grid overlay; snake segments scale with depth; particles and food bob in world space; all geometry depth-sorted
- Ghost mode colors: head white, body cyan; reduced opacity with shimmer effect
- CRT scanlines overlay (3px dark lines) across entire page

**Effects & Feedback:**
- Particle burst: 14 pink/yellow radiating particles (~450ms) on food/power-up eat
- Death animation: 650ms flashing (80ms intervals) red/white segments
- Audio: start (660Hz, 880Hz), food pitch rises with score, death (220→140→80Hz sawtooth descending)

**UI & States:**
- States: 'start', 'playing', 'paused', 'dying' (650ms), 'gameover'
- HUD: score (green glow, left), power badges (center), hi-score (pink glow, right); mode tag (bottom-right, "VIEW 2D/2.5D/3D")
- Start screen: pulsing "NEON SNAKE" title (green+pink), mode selector buttons, "INSERT COIN" button (yellow, blinking), control hints
- Pause screen: "PAUSED" title, power-up hints, "PRESS P TO RESUME" prompt
- Game Over screen: final score, best score, "NEW HI-SCORE" badge (if applicable)
- Space/Enter starts from start/game-over; arrow/WASD auto-starts from start screen
- P toggles pause; pause freezes rendering but power-up timers continue

**3D Implementation (canvas/WebGL, no THREE.js):**
- Self-contained perspective math: camera orbit, orthographic projection, depth sorting
- Depth fade: far objects darken toward black; near objects bright
- Render depth-sorted drawables (snake, food, particles) to ensure correct layering
